## Proof

**Setup.** We have 2015 points $A_0,\dots,A_{2014}$ forming a regular 2014-simplex inscribed in the unit sphere of $\mathbb{R}^{2014}$, so $|A_i|=1$ for all $i$, and the centroid is the origin $O$ (the center of the circumsphere of a regular simplex coincides with its centroid). Hence $\sum_{i=0}^{2014} A_i = 0$.

**Key identity.** For any point $P$ and points $A_i$ with centroid $G$:
$$\sum_i |P-A_i|^2 = n|P-G|^2 + \sum_i |A_i-G|^2, \quad n=2015.$$
With $G=O=0$ and $|A_i|=1$:
$$S = \sum_{i=0}^{2014}|P-A_i|^2 = 2015\,|P|^2 + 2015 = 2015\bigl(|P|^2+1\bigr).$$

**Computing $|P|^2$.** The 2014 coordinates of $P$ alternate $20,14,20,14,\dots$, giving 1007 coordinates equal to 20 and 1007 equal to 14:
$$|P|^2 = 1007\cdot 20^2 + 1007\cdot 14^2 = 1007(400+196)=1007\cdot 596 = 600172.$$

**Final sum.**
$$S = 2015(600172+1)=2015\cdot 600173.$$
$$2015\cdot 600173 = 2015\cdot 600000 + 2015\cdot 173 = 1{,}209{,}000{,}000 + 348{,}595 = 1{,}209{,}348{,}595.$$

**Remainder modulo $1{,}000{,}000$:**
$$1{,}209{,}348{,}595 \bmod 1{,}000{,}000 = 348{,}595.$$

The remainder is $\boxed{348595}$.

